course: dictionary
lesson: 2577
title: Democrat, with a small d or a big D
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can change meaning when it has a capital letter. A capital letter often shows a special name, such as a party, a country or a person. «In the USA they are the Democrats (whose cartoon symbol is a donkey) and the Republicans (an elephant).» Here Democrats with a capital D is the name of one real party in one country.
explain: Read the words around the word first. Words like «party», «votes», «election» and «states» are clues that the topic is politics. A democrat with a small d is anyone who believes in democracy, where people choose their leaders by voting and everyone has equal rights.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «The Democrats are one of the two biggest parties in the United States» still make sense? Yes, so the capital D is a name. If your meaning makes the sentence strange, try another one.
fact: A democrat (small d) is a person who believes in democracy: people choose their leaders by voting, and everyone has equal rights.
fact: A Democrat (capital D) is a member or supporter of the Democratic Party, one of the two biggest parties in the United States.
fact: The other big party in the United States is the Republican Party.
fact: On election maps, Democrats are usually shown in blue and Republicans in red.
fact: The donkey symbol of the Democrats comes from old newspaper cartoons.
exercise: In «In the USA, the Democrats and the Republicans are the two biggest parties», what are the Democrats? | A kind of map | *One of the two biggest parties in the United States | A country in Europe | A type of animal
exercise: On an election map, which colour usually shows the Democrats? | Red | *Blue | Yellow | Green
exercise: A democrat with a small d believes in what? | *Democracy, where people choose leaders by voting | Maps of the USA | Cartoons | Donkeys
test: Which symbol is used for the Democrats in cartoons? | A lion | *A donkey | A horse | An elephant
test: Which party is often called "the third party" in the UK? | The Conservatives | *The Liberal Democrats | Labour | The Republicans
exam: What does a small d democrat mean? | A person who only supports one US party | A donkey in a cartoon | *Anyone who believes in democracy, in any country | A red state on a map
